                      ENOENT                        tests assert on

The Step 1 log is the OLD suite, whose expectations were prose ("expect 0")
rather than computed. That is the point: a suite that reports in sentences can
print "expect 0", get -1, and still say PASS, and it cannot report anything at
all once its own printing is charged.

EXEC COST. First measured by hand in step1_exec_cost.log (group 9 exec'ing a
group-0 /echo used 7 = 5 exec + 2 writes; group 0 exec'ing its own used 2 = 0 +
the child's two writes; group 10 with budget 4 refused and used 0), and now
asserted as deltas inside Test 1 against a silent binary (/sync):

    T1 foreign exec charge = 5           T1 own-group exec charge = 0
    T1 foreign exec counted = 1          T1 own-group exec skipped the bucket = 0
    T1 foreign exec ran = 0 (exit)       T1 own-group exec ran = 0 (exit)

and in Test 7 against a closed bucket:

    T7 denied exec returns the sentinel = 10 (the child's exit code for -42)
    T7 denied exec did not run the binary
    T7 denied exec spent nothing / granted nothing / refused = 1

"ran = 0" is the assertion that makes the charge assertion worth reading: a zero
delta is only evidence if the operation actually happened. That distinction was
learned the hard way (section 5, the mkfs underscore rule). The property that
matters most here is the last block: a denial cannot be used to burn budget,
because the charge is refused before anything is deducted.

TEST 1, COST MATRIX - every row of section 2, each asserted as a budget delta
and each cross-checked against the operation actually happening (T1 console 1,
own-group write 0, other-group write 3, unlink 10 with the file really gone,
foreign exec 5, own-group exec 0). 17 assertions. One of them is visible in the
log as a stray character: the line reads "x[PASS] T1 console write charge = 1",
because that test really does write a character to the console with the charged
printf. The charged output path still exists and is still charged; only the
reporting path became free.

TEST 2, THE TWO SEMANTICS THAT ARE EASIEST TO GET WRONG:

    a lower ceiling clamps the held budget          100 -> 20, not 20 -> 50
    T2 BLOCK ticks waited                           100
    T2 BLOCK waited unlink counted as ONE episode   blocked delta = 1
    T2 FAIL denial returns the sentinel             -42
    T2 FAIL denial spent nothing / did not block    used delta 0, blocked delta 0
    T2 FAIL denial ticks waited                     0

TEST 3, BOUNDARIES. setgroup(-1), setgroup(NGROUP), a bad gid, a negative max, a
negative refill and an unknown mode each return -1, and setgroup(NGROUP-1)
returns 0. Two of the four cases that used to be a hang or a false negative are
the interesting ones:

    exactly affordable (max 10, cost 10)   ran, drained to 0, spent exactly 10
    price above the ceiling, BLOCK mode    denied (-42), blocked delta 0
    no accrual and an empty bucket, BLOCK  denied (-42), blocked delta 0
    refill after 1100 idle ticks           caps at exactly max = 100
    a line printed with a closed bucket    spent 0, granted 0, reported 1

The middle two are the Step 2 fix to charge(): BLOCK is only a wait if the
bucket can eventually reach the price. Sleeping forever on a price that can
never be afforded is a hang, not a throttle, so it is refused the way FAIL
refuses it.

Honest caveat on one of these assertions: "T3 a rejected setgroup left the group
alone" checks only that setgroup(-5) returns -1. It never reads the process's
group back, so it would pass even if a rejected call had moved the process. The
thing that actually proves the property is the source: kernel/sysproc.c:120
returns -1 before the `p->gid = gid` assignment on line 123. To make the test
prove it too, a readback of the calling process's group is needed, and there is
no getgroup() syscall yet.

TEST 4, FORK BOMB, AND WHY IT IS NOW TWO MEASUREMENTS. Group 5, 30 tokens,
refill 0, FAIL, 10 children each attempting one unlink:

    kernel granted 3 / refused 7        (from getbudgetstat)
    children that deleted 3 / denied 7  (from the exit statuses)
    total spend equals the ceiling      used delta = 30, budget = 0

The kernel's counters and the children's own exit codes are independent readings
of the same fact; before Step 2 the second one could not be printed at all.

TEST 5, ISOLATION UNDER CONCURRENCY. Group 6 (100, BLOCK) and group 7 (30, FAIL)
hammer simultaneously, neither waited on: 5 granted / 0 waited / 50 spent versus
3 granted / 2 refused / 30 spent, plus "the throttled group did not tax the
other" and each process's own count agreeing with the kernel's.

TEST 6, THE STAIRCASE AND THE FLAT LINE - the lab's headline graph, from [DATA]
rows the kernel produced, not from an axhline:

    [DATA],BLOCK,1204,0   [DATA],FAIL,1404,0
    [DATA],BLOCK,1204,1   [DATA],FAIL,1404,1
    [DATA],BLOCK,1204,2   [DATA],FAIL,1404,2
    [DATA],BLOCK,1204,3   [DATA],FAIL,1404,3   <- 3 done, then denial is instant
    [DATA],BLOCK,1304,4   [DATA],FAIL,1404,3   <- refused, file still there
    [DATA],BLOCK,1404,5   [DATA],FAIL,1424,3   <- the test's own pause(20)

    BLOCK: 5 deletions, 5 granted, 0 refused, 2 blocked episodes, 200 ticks
    FAIL : 3 deletions, 3 granted, 2 refused, 0 blocked, 40 ticks (< 1 period)

Same price, same bucket, opposite shape: BLOCK steps one unlink per refill
period, FAIL flatlines at the ceiling. The 4th and 5th BLOCK rows are the two
unlinks that had to wait for accrual, and n_blocked = 2 says the kernel knows it
waited exactly twice.

TEST 7, DENIALS VS REAL ERRORS, AND THE FREE PATH. A denied exec returns the
sentinel and spends nothing; an unlink of a missing file returns -1 - not the
sentinel - and IS charged 10, because the kernel cannot know an attempt is
harmless until it has run it; and uptime, getbudgetstat and report with a closed
bucket move no grant counters while n_reported advances ("one line is one
report = 1", "bytes reported with a closed bucket = 46").

SELF-REPORTED TABLE AT THE END OF THE GREEN RUN (the REPORTED column is what
Step 2 added; group 6's 0 is its child, which never printed):

      GID BUDGET/MAX REFILL  MODE  ALLOWED BLOCKED REFUSED REPORTED
        0    100/  100     10 BLOCK       19        0        0         4
        1    100/  100   1000 BLOCK        4        0        0        18
        3      0/    0      0 FAIL         1        0        3        22
        4      0/   50      0 FAIL         3        1        1        25
